cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GyroOS: Execution Architecture for Slice-based, Deviation-aware, Stability-driven Computation"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Gyro Logic Lab"
    given-names: ""

abstract: >
  GyroOS is a computational system that implements Gyro Logic as an execution architecture.
  It operates on multiple slice-based representations, explicitly models deviation (Δ) between observations,
  and evaluates stability as tolerance under inconsistency.
  Instead of assuming a single correct representation, GyroOS performs selection among competing views,
  enabling computation under unavoidable deviation.

keywords:
  - gyro logic
  - stability
  - deviation
  - slice
  - dynamic systems
  - computation
  - identity
  - observation

license: CC-BY-4.0
